<title>BELGIUM: EU VETS POLISH TELEVISION JOINT VENTURE.</title>
<headline>EU VETS POLISH TELEVISION JOINT VENTURE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had started a routine antitrust review of a deal under which newly created television group CLT-UFA and a unit of Universal Studies Inc acquire joint control of RTL 7, a Polish-language TV broadcasting joint venture.</p>
<p>CLT-UFA is controlled by Audiofina and Bertelsmann.</p>
<p>Universal Studios TV Channel Poland BV is a subsidiary of Universal Studios which in turn is controlled by the Seagram Company LTD.</p>
<p>Under EU rules, the Commission has one month to complete its investigation and either clear the deal or start a detailed second stage investigation. Most deals are cleared after one month.</p>
</text>
